+
+## DeepSeek review input cap
+
+DeepSeek code, scaffold and approved-plan reviews share a 131,072-token (128k)
+input cap, with 8,192 tokens reserved separately for the response: 139,264 tokens
+of native context. The exact counter includes the rendered instructions,
+requirements, work specification and selected evidence before the model swap.
+Requests above the cap are split and recounted; every coverage part must pass.
+The preparer's own input budget remains separate from the reviewer's budget.
+
+The native engine, prefill buffers, memory planner and launch context use the
+same cap. The checkpoint's original 65,536-position RoPE scaling parameter is
+unchanged. This is a configured limit, not a new long-context performance result;
+older 32k benchmark and qualification records retain their measured scope.
+
+128k cap validation: code and scaffold dispatch tests accept the exact input
+boundary and reject oversized mandatory context before inference. Native
+counter tests count real rendered prompts at 131,072 and 131,073 tokens;
+allocation, prefill and session fixtures also pass. The CUDA binary builds.
+This change does not include a live 128k model benchmark. Existing processes
+pick up the new profile and executable on their next restart.
